 "intro": {
  "title": "SOUNDING DEEP GATE",
  "lines": [
   "The stair from the spire came out in the dark.",
   "Below it is a bowl of lamps, and a city built round the bowl."
  ]
 },
 "outro": "The door in the drum opens on a stair wide enough for two carts.",
 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "start",
   "at": [11, 22],
   "radius": 4,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "Dark. The tin on the floor is a Marrow tin with the label gone. Somebody carried it this far down and put it where it would be found."
  },
  {
   "id": "lamp",
   "at": [19, 29],
   "radius": 3,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "The lantern is L. Gaunts and Gills find you by eye: from 6 metres with it out, 24 with it lit. Tollbearers follow the Hush and do not care about light."
  },
  {
   "id": "mouth",
   "at": [31, 39],
   "radius": 3,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "The tunnel opens on a bowl lit in rings. The far side is houses stacked up to the roof, a window lit in every one. There are Vael on every terrace, walking."
  },
  {
   "id": "folk",
   "at": [38, 32],
   "radius": 4,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "None of them has a bell. They are carrying baskets and cord and they have not looked up. Do not shoot what is walking."
  },
  {
   "id": "zealot",
   "at": [31, 44],
   "radius": 4,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "One on the east terraces is standing still with a lance as long as a mast. Armoured, and its feet apart, the way a man stands who means to stay."
  },
  {
   "id": "ramp",
   "at": [36, 50],
   "radius": 3,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "The west ramp is the only way down. A Bulwark Shell is on it: the plate on its front stops a shot. Hit it from the side, or when it opens to strike."
  },
  {
   "id": "plate",
   "at": [46, 57],
   "radius": 3,
   "speaker": "RINGING PLATE",
